[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says the date reports are one issue with one fix queued. The desk's own
table below says otherwise: the reports merged into it have more than one cause. They were merged on
subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and "wrong date" is a
subject that more than one bug produces.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is the parser fix. It does nothing for the <code>hint</code> reports: they
now have their own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Original desk view, export of 2026-10-04. The table shows two causes, and each now has a ticket:

- the `parser` row, with the reports in its footnote → [#1 Shared date parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-4/issues/1)
- the `hint` row, "no ticket of its own" in the export, which predates #2 → [#2 booking-v3 form gives day-first tenants an MM/DD/YYYY hint](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-4/issues/2)

The footnote is an annotation inside `parser`, not a third cause and not extra reports: those reports
stay counted where they are filed. Their bodies describe a one-day move, not a swap; the desk should
check them when the parser fix ships.

## What each problem is

**`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and month
swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July.

**`hint`** — `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as told,
and the form reads the value the tenant's way. Same symptom as `parser`, different code, different
fix.

## For the desk

- Merge into a ticket only reports with the same cause, not the same subject.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser; place a report by its tenant, as the table does.

